# FastAPI Blog

A small FastAPI learning project that serves a sample blog post as HTML and exposes the posts through a JSON API. The posts are currently stored in memory and are defined in `main.py`.

## Features

- FastAPI application with automatic API documentation
- `GET /posts` HTML page showing the first blog post
- `GET /` alternate HTML route for the same page, hidden from the API schema
- `GET /api/posts` endpoint for the sample blog posts
- Development server with hot reload

## Setup

Create and activate a virtual environment from this directory:

```bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
```

Install the project dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Run the Server

Start the development server with hot reload:

```bash
fastapi dev main.py
```

The API is available at:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Use `Ctrl+C` to stop the server.

## API Endpoints

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/posts` | Renders the first blog post as HTML |
| `GET` | `/` | Renders the same HTML page; excluded from generated docs |
| `GET` | `/api/posts` | Returns the sample blog posts |

The `/` and `/posts` routes are mapped to the same function. The root route uses `include_in_schema=False`, so it does not appear in Swagger UI or ReDoc.

## API Documentation

FastAPI generates interactive documentation automatically:

- Swagger UI: [http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs)
- ReDoc: [http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc](http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc)

## Learning Notes

This project is an early step toward a complete blog backend. Current topics include route decorators, mapping multiple paths to one function, HTML responses with `HTMLResponse`, and controlling which routes appear in the generated schema. Future improvements may include request and response models, create/update/delete operations, validation, a database, authentication, and tests.